f41510b09bb5","event_uuid":"6c9bb76a-c0ae-4c05-9fb2-a88ea238162c","position":{"commit_sha":"28abb5247030e022b46f2e841ad661fe88d306d8","position":"1794263366432139001-6c9bb76a-c0ae-4c05-9fb2-a88ea238162c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"4ff0a7bc5bc900912ee204904df1600eb96d084b94021d96feaf0c73d554841d","event_uuid":"37af98ba-82ce-45aa-b91b-0075485d8c08","position":{"commit_sha":"28abb5247030e022b46f2e841ad661fe88d306d8","position":"1794263377106742001-37af98ba-82ce-45aa-b91b-0075485d8c08"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"b9ed1ec923319bb0034a0c4540a24ec4bc44453b05573e3b2f7a9867c68ab574","event_uuid":"497222c0-f9ae-4a00-9f56-681dbb8be387","position":{"commit_sha":"e5676dfc208465966c2b3d5507b43e0c6536cee2","position":"1794266126018824001-497222c0-f9ae-4a00-9f56-681dbb8be387"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-308_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"a85e3cd3-9e61-4f25-9de4-cd740e853b4d","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Model-call audit against the 5.5 API changes (2026-11-09 PST)\n\nScope: every model call path in `src/rebar` — the pydantic-ai runner (`llm/runner.py`, `llm/structured_run.py`, `llm/agent_call.py`), provider construction (`llm/anthropic_model.py`, `llm/bedrock_model.py`, `llm/providers.py`), and the two raw-SDK sites (`anthropic_model._move_unsupported_beta_create_kwargs`, `evals/provider_parity.probe_slot`). Every gate pass, the completion verifier, code review, scan-spec and the workflow steps reach the model only through `PydanticAIRunner.run`, so the runner rows cover them.\n\n### Wire probe (riskiest assumption)\n\nOne short call per case, each 5.5 model, each provider (Bedrock `us.anthropic.*-5-5` via boto3 `converse`; direct `claude-*-5-5` via the Anthropic SDK):\n\n| model | bare | `temperature=0` | explicit `effort` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Opus 5.5 (Bedrock, direct) | accepted, `end_turn` | 400 \"`temperature` is deprecated for this model.\" | accepted (`high`) |\n| Sonnet 5.5 (Bedrock, direct) | accepted, `end_turn` | 400, same message | accepted (`high`) |\n| Haiku 5.5 (Bedrock, direct) | accepted, `end_turn` | 400, same message | accepted (`medium`) |\n\n### Findings\n\n| # | API change | site | finding | disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | forced `tool_choice` `any`/`tool` 400s (Opus, Sonnet) | `structured.output_mode` (`llm/structured.py:149`), `runner.py:273` | rebar never forces a tool. Structured output is `NativeOutput` or `PromptedOutput` only; no `ToolOutput` exists in the stack; agentic loops use pydantic-ai's default `auto`. `git grep tool_choice -- src` finds only comments. | not affected |\n| 2 | thinking cannot be disabled (Opus 5.5) | `RunRequest.thinking` (`runner.py:93`) | no caller sets thinking, and no `anthropic_thinking`/`thinking` setting is sent anywhere, so rebar never sends `{type: \"disabled\"}` or a budget. Opus 5.5 therefore runs adaptive thinking by default. Claude output stays `PromptedOutput` (`capabilities._REBAR_OVERRIDES`), which is compatible with thinking. | not affected |\n| 3 | `temperature`/`top_p`/`top_k` rejected | `structured_run.build_model_settings` (`:400-404`); Pass-2 verify and `completion.py:397` set `temperature=0`; `evals/plan_replay/tier1.py:110`, `tier2.py:391,580` | **affected**: the 4.x verifier path sends `temperature=0`, which 400s on every 5.5 model (probe above). `top_p`/`top_k` are never sent. | **fixed**: every 5.5 id (bare, `us.`, `global.`) gets `supports_temperature: False` in `_MODEL_ID_CAPABILITY_OVERRIDES`, so the builder withdraws it on both providers (pinned by `test_five_five_ids_withdraw_temperature_and_pin_effort` and `test_the_temperature_withdrawal_is_symmetric_across_provider_arms`). |\n| 4 | assistant prefill rejected | runner, structured stack | no call ends `messages` on an assistant turn: rebar passes no `message_history`, and the prompted path's single bounded retry appends the validation error as a user turn. | not affected |\n| 5 | Opus 5.5 / Haiku 5.5 default `effort` to `medium` | `build_model_settings` | **affected**: rebar sent no effort, so 4.x ran at the API default `high`; on 5.5 the same request would silently run Opus at `medium`. | **fixed**: a per-model `effort` on `ModelCapabilities` (`high` Opus/Sonnet 5.5, `medium` Haiku 5.5), emitted as `anthropic_effort` and as Bedrock `additionalModelRequestFields.output_config.effort`. `test_the_pinned_effort_reaches_the_wire_on_both_provider_arms` captures both providers' payloads and asserts `output_config.effort == \"high\"`. |\n| 6 | `refusal` stop reason (new on Haiku; Opus/Sonnet classifiers broadened) | `failure.py:263,369-375` | pydantic-ai maps Anthropic `refusal` and Bedrock `content_filtered`/`guardrail_intervened` to `finish_reason=content_filter`; rebar classifies that as a complete-but-unusable turn (`errors.py:203`), never a PASS. Bedrock Converse's `StopReason` enum (botocore 1.43.75) has no `refusal` member, so a Bedrock refusal arrives as `content_filtered` and takes the same path. | not affected |\n| 7 | output ceiling / window | `review_kernel/verify.py::MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS`, `model_classes.MODEL_WINDOW_LADDER` | 5.5 rows added (128K output, 1M window for all three). The ladder's 4.x rows were removed; the conservative window for an unlocated model is kept at 200K as `UNLOCATED_MODEL_WINDOW_TOKENS` rather than derived from the (now all-1M) ladder minimum. | fixed |\n| 8 | prompt-cache minimum | `capabilities._MODEL_CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS` | 5.5 models cache from 512 tokens (Opus 4.8: 1024; Haiku 4.5: 4096). | fixed: three rows at 512 |\n| 9 | raw SDK sites | `anthropic_model._move_unsupported_beta_create_kwargs`; `provider_parity.probe_slot` | the first only relocates sampling kwargs the runner already withdraws; the second is the operator probe and intentionally sends `temperature=0` to measure the rejection. | not affected |\n| 10 | pydantic-ai 1.107.9 profile | `pydantic_ai/profiles/anthropic.py::anthropic_model_profile` | does not list 5.5 ids, so its profile claims forced tool choice supported and sampling allowed. Neither is reachable (rows 1 and 3), and `anthropic_effort` is copied to `output_config.effort` unconditionally (`models/anthropic.py:1960-1978`), so no profile override is needed. 1.107.10 is a security-only release. | not affected |\n\nNo incompatibility needed a change outside this ticket's seams, so no bug was filed from the audit.","timestamp":1794266126018824001}],"created_at":1794255504985466001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c77b31e4-fefb-4a94-937f-1bd397e8d31f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"81a1-0fc3-496d-4a00"},{"link_uuid":"fd39bf20-66ca-4456-a8a9-fc5288c09187","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"eeb7-c365-6e95-4802"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe project pins Opus 4.8, Sonnet 4.6 and Haiku 4.5 (`rebar.toml`, `.github/llm-providers/*.toml`). Bedrock (896586841071/us-east-1) serves the 5.5 inference profiles. The epic lands this first, on the current engine.\n\nA bare id swap is unsafe. On 5.5: forced `tool_choice` `any`/`tool` returns 400 (Opus, Sonnet); thinking cannot be disabled (Opus); non-default sampling parameters return 400; assistant prefill returns 400; `effort` defaults to `medium` on Opus and Haiku. `pydantic-ai-slim` 1.107.9 (`profiles/anthropic.py::anthropic_model_profile`) does not list 5.5 ids, so its profile wrongly allows sampling for them.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Riskiest assumption first (measured).** rebar's calls carry no forced tool choice, thinking toggle or prefill, so only sampling and effort need code: `structured.output_mode` (`src/rebar/llm/structured.py:149`) returns only `NativeOutput` or `PromptedOutput`; `capabilities._REBAR_OVERRIDES` (`capabilities.py:214`) pins Claude to `PromptedOutput` (no tool, no prefill); no caller sets `RunRequest.thinking=True` (`runner.py:93`). The wire behaviour was probed on 2026-11-09 with one short call per case on each 5.5 model, on Bedrock (boto3 `converse`) and direct Anthropic (SDK): a bare call is accepted, `temperature=0` is rejected (400 \"`temperature` is deprecated for this model\"), and `effort` (Bedrock `additionalModelRequestFields={\"output_config\": {\"effort\": ...}}`, direct `output_config.effort`) is accepted. The results are re-recorded on this ticket in Step 1 from the same calls.\n\n**Ids and tables.** Replace 4.x ids with the 5.5 ids verbatim (direct `claude-opus-5-5`, `claude-sonnet-5-5`, `claude-haiku-5-5`; Bedrock `us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5`, `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5`, `us.anthropic.claude-haiku-5-5`). These are exactly what `aws bedrock list-inference-profiles --profile frontier --region us-east-1` returned on 2026-11-09; unlike Haiku 4.5's dated profile (`capabilities.py:246`), Haiku 5.5's has no suffix. They go in the three toml files, `config.DEFAULT_MODEL`/`VERIFIER_DEFAULT_MODEL` (`src/rebar/llm/config.py:61,67`), `model_classes.TRIVIAL_DEFAULT_MODEL` (`model_classes.py:45`), `bedrock_model.DEFAULT_BEDROCK_MODEL_ID` and `provider_parity.CLASS_SLOTS`. The per-model tables are ADDITIVE, so an explicitly configured 4.x model keeps working: 5.5 rows are added to `MODEL_WINDOW_LADDER` (`model_classes.py:62-66`; all 1M) and `review_kernel/verify.py::MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS` (`:294-297`; all 128K), and 4.x rows stay. The deploy defaults in `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:97-99` and the alarm `ModelId` dimensions in `infra/terraform/monitoring_eb6e.tf:80-135` change in the same commit, because `tests/unit/test_reviewbot_bedrock_cutover.py` requires the compose slots to equal `bedrock.toml` byte for byte and the alarms to watch exactly those ids. The post-deploy check that Bedrock publishes metrics under those ids is the sibling task `itchy-neutral-whooper`. `sizing._RUNG_CLASSES` (`plan_review/sizing.py:240`) keys on family substrings; no change.\n\n**Sampling.** Add each 5.5 id (bare, `us.`, `global.`) to `_MODEL_ID_CAPABILITY_OVERRIDES` (`capabilities.py:223`) with `supports_temperature: False`, the mechanism already used for Opus 4.7/4.8, so `structured_run.build_model_settings` (`:400-404`) omits Pass-2 `temperature=0`.\n\n**Effort, explicit.** rebar sends no `effort` today (no `effort`/`output_config` key is set under `src/rebar/llm`), so Opus 4.8 and Sonnet 4.6 run at the API default, which Anthropic's documentation gives as `high`. Opus 5.5 defaults to `medium`, so to keep the frontier and standard passes at today's depth one per-model table beside the overrides pins `high` for Opus 5.5 and Sonnet 5.5. Haiku 4.5 had no effort parameter at all (it ran without thinking), so there is no prior level to preserve; Haiku 5.5 is pinned at its documented default, `medium`, which is already more reasoning than Haiku 4.5 used. `structured_run.build_model_settings` and `agent_call.build_agent_kwargs` send it through pydantic-ai 1.107.9's provider-scoped settings: `anthropic_effort` on direct Anthropic, which `AnthropicModel` copies into `output_config.effort` unconditionally (`pydantic_ai/models/anthropic.py:1960-1978`; the profile flag only gates the thinking-derived fallback), and `bedrock_additional_model_requests_fields={\"output_config\": {\"effort\": ...}}` on Bedrock (`pydantic_ai/models/bedrock.py:338`, merged at `:706`). No profile override is needed: rebar never requests a forced tool, and sampling is withdrawn by the override table above.\n\n**Cache minimum.** Add the three direct 5.5 ids to `_MODEL_CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS` (`capabilities.py:38`) at 512.\n\n**Audit.** Walk every model call site (`runner.py`, `structured_run.py`, `agent_call.py`, `anthropic_model.py`, `bedrock_model.py`, `providers.py` (read only), `review_kernel/`, `plan_review/passes.py`, `workflow/`) against the five changes plus the `refusal` stop reason, and record one row per check (site, finding, fix or \"not affected\") as a ticket comment. Anything needing more than these seams is filed as a bug linked `discovered_from`.\n\nThese seams already shape every call, so correcting them corrects every pass without touching the passes. The eval-spec `model:` pins move in the sibling task `real-pubescent-turnstone` (see links).\n\n## Scope\n\n- rebar.toml, .github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml, .github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml\n- src/rebar/llm/config.py, model_classes.py, capabilities.py, structured_run.py, agent_call.py, bedrock_model.py\n- src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py\n- src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py, src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/provider_parity_results.json\n- infra/compose/docker-compose.yml, infra/terraform/monitoring_eb6e.tf\n- tests: the five files a measured spike showed break (all edits applied, 220 test files that name a 4.x id, a changed constant, or a provider/compose/alarm file run: 24 failures in these five, 3,924 passes, including `test_reviewbot_bedrock_cutover.py`): tests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py, test_model_classes.py, test_plan_review.py, test_provider_parity.py, test_verifier_class.py; plus new cases in tests/unit/test_capabilities.py and tests/unit/test_settings_builders_seam.py.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: each 5.5 id reports `supports_temperature=False` and a 512 cache minimum; a 5.5 Bedrock request carries `output_config.effort` and no `temperature`; a direct one carries `anthropic_effort`.\n- Edge: an unmapped id keeps family defaults (no effort sent, temperature kept); `sizing` maps `us.anthropic.claude-haiku-5-5` to `trivial`.\n- Live: provider-parity probe and full run once on 4.x before the change and once on 5.5 after, `AWS_PROFILE=frontier-bedrock`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `git grep -nE 'claude-(opus-4-8|sonnet-4-6|haiku-4-5)' -- rebar.toml .github/llm-providers src/rebar/llm/config.py src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py infra/compose/docker-compose.yml infra/terraform/monitoring_eb6e.tf` prints nothing, and `TRIVIAL_DEFAULT_MODEL` is `\"claude-haiku-5-5\"` (the files where ids are replaced; the per-model tables keep their 4.x rows by design).\n- [ ] The model-call audit is a ticket comment with one row per call site and API change.\n- [ ] Every incompatibility the audit finds is fixed here or filed as a linked bug.\n- [ ] The capability and settings-builder tests under Testing pass.\n- [ ] A ticket comment records, for each 5.5 model on Bedrock and on direct Anthropic, that a bare call and a call with the pinned `effort` are accepted and a `temperature=0` call is rejected.\n- [ ] The before and after provider-parity results are recorded in a ticket comment.\n- [ ] The 5.5 provider-parity run reports `invalid: false` for both slots.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"rebar.toml","reason":"5.5 ids"},{"path":".github/llm-providers/bedrock.toml","reason":"5.5 profiles"},{"path":".github/llm-providers/anthropic.toml","reason":"5.5 direct ids"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/config.py","reason":"default models"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py","reason":"trivial default, 5.5 window rows"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py","reason":"5.5 overrides, effort table, cache minimum"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py","reason":"explicit effort"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py","reason":"explicit effort on agentic calls"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/bedrock_model.py","reason":"default Bedrock id"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py","reason":"5.5 max-output rows"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/provider_parity.py","reason":"parity slots"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/provider_parity_results.json","reason":"re-recorded run"},{"path":"infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","reason":"deploy model defaults"},{"path":"infra/terraform/monitoring_eb6e.tf","reason":"alarm ModelId dimensions"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py","reason":"pinned ids/values or new 5.5 cases"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_model_classes.py","reason":"pinned ids/values or new 5.5 cases"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review.py","reason":"pinned ids/values or new 5.5 cases"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py","reason":"pinned ids/values or new 5.5 cases"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_verifier_class.py","reason":"pinned ids/values or new 5.5 cases"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_capabilities.py","reason":"pinned ids/values or new 5.5 cases"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_settings_builders_seam.py","reason":"pinned ids/values or new 5.5 cases"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"],["relates_to","81a1-0fc3-496d-4a00"],["relates_to","eeb7-c365-6e95-4802"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"6c9bb76a-c0ae-4c05-9fb2-a88ea238162c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"7341-7f22-b13a-442c","ticket_type":"task","title":"Upgrade configured models to Opus 5.5 / Sonnet 5.5 / Haiku 5.5 and audit every model call","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["30c1691b-b9f1-444c-ae67-c5baf1511cff","5120f59c-6d6d-4b95-a7d6-8e0d288e58cc","d6c05322-0e0c-4272-b8c3-6fbba388cc48","32f98e1c-6519-4571-9ec0-58829dd1f8d8","c77b31e4-fefb-4a94-937f-1bd397e8d31f","5ec3014f-e49f-4e75-bf88-97e40e521a4f","fd39bf20-66ca-4456-a8a9-fc5288c09187","7b691d94-f3a8-47a0-b918-c19a6e325c9a","d6f11f54-2631-4db9-b811-dc88d2657fed","d23db4a0-1b8a-4875-b40d-6944bea66ca8","27065a59-fa6a-4084-9986-d3befef20c29","8ec31b16-a061-40de-8513-456d172ed978","f0ceb54c-1cc4-48eb-81b3-3464060e0a94","50549256-197f-4b11-95ab-25531fa44c18","f742c066-5a97-46a7-9a01-cce4633af62a","6c9bb76a-c0ae-4c05-9fb2-a88ea238162c","37af98ba-82ce-45aa-b91b-0075485d8c08","497222c0-f9ae-4a00-9f56-681dbb8be387"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794266126018824002,"uuid":"b94aaf69-0b15-460d-ab91-25683a67b689"}